    2. For each chain, assign square sizes (from {2,3,5}) to its sprites and unique 2-color checkerboard patterns.
    3. Build the settled (output) layout right-to-left against column 14. For each chain, place the rightmost-row-overlapping sprite flush to col 14, then stack each predecessor flush left of the sprite it overlaps with. Ensure no pixel overlap between chains (row-disjoint) and all sprites fit within the 15x15 grid.
    4. Derive input by shifting each sprite leftward by a random amount (1-11 cols), preserving the relative ordering that the solver's rightward gravity would restore. Ensure no two sprites overlap in the input and all remain within grid bounds.
    5. Validate: run solver on input and confirm it reproduces the output.
